(IJdo, 2015) found Na$_{2}$U$_{2}$O$_{7}$ in two forms: \begin{itemize} \item The low temperature \href{current_web_home_dir/A2B7C2_mP44_14_ace_7e_2e-001}{$\alpha$-Na$_{2}$U$_{2}$O$_{7}$} (this structure), and \item The high-temperature \href{current_web_home_dir/A2B7C2_mC44_12_abh_3i2j_ei-001}{$\beta$-Na$_{2}$U$_{2}$O$_{7}$} phase. \end{itemize} ~ \vspace{-.25in} 
 The data for $\alpha$-Na$_{2}$U$_{2}$O$_{7}$ was taken at 293K, and the data for $\beta$-Na$_{2}$U$_{2}$O$_{7}$ was taken at 773K.  The exact transition temperature was not determined. 
 (IJdo, 2015) presented the structural information for $\alpha$-Na$_{2}$U$_{2}$O$_{7}$ in the $P2_{1}/a$ setting of space group \#14.  We used AFLOW to transform it to the standard $P2_{1}/c$ setting.  This involves a considerable reordering of the primitive vectors.
